  "scientific_interpretation": {
    "bins": "Aggregate frozen forecast bins contain 115/114/114/114/115 players and 55/77/93/107/115 observed pairs. Observed means are monotone (-3.381889, -2.384373, -0.428387, 1.726902, 6.184429), supporting ordinal separation among observed players.",
    "category_evidence": "All nine category slopes are positive and all nine slope intervals lie below 1. Ratio-impact rank evidence is weakest (FG Spearman 0.651528; FT 0.616501). FT observed bin means have one local middle-bin reversal; this is descriptive evidence, not a preregistered veto.",
    "primary_aggregate": "447 observed-player pairs; intercept 0.275893 [0.066228, 0.471567], slope 0.814927 [0.754176, 0.876818], +1 anchor 1.090820, +2 anchor 1.905747, Spearman 0.837730, MAE 1.833268, RMSE 2.369671. The interval excludes ideal slope 1 and the intercept interval excludes 0, so magnitudes are materially compressed and offset on this held-out carry-forward benchmark.",
    "scope": "The evidence validates the frozen deterministic transform and supports projection-relative ordinal/descriptive scoring. It does not validate current Basketball Monster forecasts, any current vendor, multi-source weights, forecast calibration, availability, expected games, replacement value for undersized pools, dollars, risk adjustment, strategy optimization, or actuation.",
    "selection": "Observation rates rise from 47.83% in the bottom aggregate bin to 100% in the top bin. The result is conditional on at least one complete 2024-25 credited appearance and cannot estimate production or availability for the 125 missing players. This strong survivor selection prevents population-wide calibration claims.",
    "sensitivities": "At 10/25/50 observed games the paired counts are 423/373/259 and slopes are 0.808599/0.808258/0.798654. Magnitude compression persists; minimum-games filtering does not explain it away."
  },
